{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py","reason":"Hosts the existing per-tool interception seam (install_error_guard rebinds mcp.tool before the registrars run); the JS-safe integer transform on tool return values belongs here, where it reaches both the content and structuredContent branches."},{"path":"src/rebar/mcp_server.py","reason":"Wires the transform in alongside install_error_guard at the build_server seam (only ~30 LOC of headroom under the 800-line cap, so no logic lands here)."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_js_safe_integers.py","reason":"New RED-first regression test: drives the real in-process MCP server on both the direct call_tool path and the registered CallToolRequest handler, asserting no integer outside the RFC 8259 interoperable range reaches the wire and that the nanosecond value round-trips losslessly."}]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1787857724501082219,"uuid":"37a7bbe5-6dc5-497c-b0ff-03566f7cae87"}